      ":question/id": "d3fa8b21-424a-595a-9e7d-f21c1e7011c1",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Simplify $\\cos(x+300^\\circ)$ using $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$. Enter signed coefficients.\n\n{{field-1}} $\\sin x+$ {{field-2}} $\\cos x$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use $\\cos(u+v)=\\cos u\\cos v-\\sin u\\sin v$ with $u=x$ and $v=300^\\circ$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos(x+300^\\circ)&=\\cos x\\cos 300^\\circ-\\sin x\\sin 300^\\circ\\\\\n&=\\cos x\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)-\\sin x\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\sin x+\\frac{1}{2}\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first blank is $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ and the second is $\\frac{1}{2}$.",
